---
title: Issue collection
layout: home
description: The archive of a letter — what it is, a form to join it, and every issue that has gone out, numbered. A newsletter's back catalogue is the best argument for subscribing to it.
eyebrow: Collections · Newsletter
source: src/components/collection.css · field.css
---
<section class="im-section im-wrap" style="padding-top: 1.5rem; --im-section-gap: 1.5rem">
	<p class="im-eyebrow">Collections · Newsletter · {{page.title}}</p>
	<p class="im-lede">{{page.description}}</p>
	<p class="doc-source"><code>{{page.source}}</code></p>
</section>

<div class="im-single im-wrap-wide" data-sidebar="on">
	<article class="im-stack" style="--im-stack-gap: 2rem">
		<header class="im-collhead im-collhead-patterned">
			<span class="im-collhead-art im-bg-lines" style="--im-art: #4ac26b" aria-hidden="true"></span>
			<p class="im-eyebrow">Newsletter</p>
			<h1 class="im-collhead-title">Field Notes</h1>
			<p class="im-collhead-text">One email when something lands — what I built, what it cost and what I got wrong. No schedule, no filler, no list swapping.</p>
			<p class="im-collhead-meta">
				<span>{{demo.issues.length}} issues</span>
				<span>4,100 readers</span>
				<a href="#issues">RSS</a>
			</p>
		</header>

		<section class="im-postcta" style="text-align: left; justify-items: stretch">
			<h2 class="im-postcta-title" style="text-wrap: pretty">Join 4,100 readers</h2>
			<p class="im-postcta-text" style="max-width: 52ch">Every issue is free and every issue stays up — the archive below is the whole of it.</p>
			{{> "components/subscribe" id="news-email" button="Subscribe"}}
		</section>

		<section class="im-section" id="issues">
			<div class="home-head"><p class="im-caption" data-index="all">Every issue</p><a class="im-card-cta" href="#issues">RSS {{> "icons/arrow-right"}}</a></div>
			<div class="im-issues">
				{{#each demo.issues}}
				<article class="im-issue">
					{{#if shot}}
						<span class="im-issue-tile im-issue-tile-shot"><img src="{{lookup ../demo.shots shot}}" alt="" loading="lazy"><b>{{n}}</b></span>
					{{else}}
						<span class="im-issue-tile"><b>{{n}}</b><strong>{{day}}</strong><span>{{month}}</span><small>{{year}}</small></span>
					{{/if}}
					<p class="im-issue-date">{{sent}}</p>
					<h3 class="im-issue-title"><a href="/collections/newsletter/issue/">{{title}}</a></h3>
					<p class="im-issue-text">{{text}}</p>
					<p class="im-issue-meta">
						<span class="im-kind" data-kind="issue">{{icon "mail"}}Issue</span>
						<span>{{words}} words</span>
						<span>{{read}} opened</span>
					</p>
				</article>
				{{/each}}
			</div>
		</section>
	</article>

	<aside>
		<div class="im-sticky-rail">
		<div class="im-widgets">
			<section class="im-widget im-widget-fill" aria-labelledby="nw-sub">
				<h2 class="im-widget-title" id="nw-sub">Subscribe</h2>
				<p class="im-widget-heading">Free. One email when something lands.</p>
				{{> "components/subscribe" id="letters-email" button="Join"}}
				<div class="im-widget-stats">
					<div><strong>4,210</strong><span>Readers</span></div>
					<div><strong>62%</strong><span>Opened</span></div>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section class="im-widget" aria-labelledby="nw-in">
				<h2 class="im-widget-title" id="nw-in">What is in one</h2>
				<ul class="im-widget-now">
					<li>{{icon "pencil"}}<span><b>One thing I built</b>, and what it cost.</span></li>
					<li>{{icon "triangle-alert"}}<span><b>One thing I got wrong</b>, in full.</span></li>
					<li>{{icon "link"}}<span><b>Three links</b> I would have sent you anyway.</span></li>
				</ul>
			</section>

			<section class="im-widget" aria-labelledby="nw-arch">
				<h2 class="im-widget-title" id="nw-arch">Every issue</h2>
				<nav class="im-widget-archive">
					{{#each demo.archive}}<a href="#issues">{{year}}<small>{{posts}} issues</small></a>{{/each}}
				</nav>
			</section>

			<section class="im-widget" aria-labelledby="nw-said">
				<h2 class="im-widget-title" id="nw-said">What a reader said</h2>
				<blockquote class="im-widget-quote">The only newsletter I read on the day it arrives.<span class="im-widget-quote-by">— a subscriber since issue 4</span></blockquote>
			</section>
			<aside class="im-ad im-ad-rectangle" aria-label="Advertisement">
				<span class="im-ad-label">Sponsored</span>
				<span class="im-ad-slot"><img src="{{demo.shots.[5]}}" alt="" loading="lazy"></span>
				<button class="im-btn im-btn-sm im-ad-remove" type="button" popovertarget="ad-gate">{{icon "circle-x"}}Remove ads</button>
			</aside>
		</div>
		</div>
	</aside>
</div>

<section class="im-section im-wrap">
	<div class="im-prose">
		<h2>Why the number is the biggest thing on the card</h2>
		<p>A newsletter's issues are navigated by <strong>number</strong>, not by title: a reader looking for "the one about the move" scrolls until a number looks familiar, and somebody who has just subscribed wants to know how many there are before they read any of them. So it is set like a number — Geist Pixel, tabular, and quiet enough that the title still wins the row.</p>
		<div class="im-table-scroll">
		<table>
			<thead><tr><th>Class</th><th></th></tr></thead>
			<tbody>
				<tr><td><code>im-issues</code></td><td>The column. Rows, not cards in a grid: an issue is a thing in a sequence.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>im-issue</code></td><td>One issue. It fills on hover, like every other card in the system.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>im-issue-tile</code></td><td>The date as a <strong>thumbnail</strong>: day, month, year on a tile, with the issue number riding its corner. A letter usually has no cover image, and a row of grey placeholders would be worse than none — but it always has a date, and a date is what a reader navigates an archive by.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>im-issue-tile-shot</code></td><td>When an issue <em>does</em> have a picture, it takes the tile's place and keeps the number. Mixing the two in one archive is fine and looks deliberate; what does not work is a placeholder standing in for a picture that was never taken.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>im-issue-num</code></td><td>The number on its own, for a list that does not want the tile.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>im-issue-date</code> · <code>-title</code> · <code>-text</code> · <code>-meta</code></td><td>When, what it was called, what was in it, and the facts under it.</td></tr>
			</tbody>
		</table>
		</div>
		<p>Under 34rem the number moves above the title, because a 3rem column beside a wrapped headline on a phone is two columns of nothing.</p>

		<h2>The signup is at the top, not the bottom</h2>
		<p>The archive is the argument for subscribing — but somebody who has already decided should not have to scroll past forty issues to do it. Form first, proof under it. The form itself is the <a href="/forms/inputs/#subscribe">subscribe component</a>, wired to Ghost's members.</p>

		<h2>In a theme</h2>
		{{{{code "hbs"}}}}
{{#get "posts" filter="tag:#issue" limit="all" order="published_at desc"}}
	<div class="im-issues">
		{{#foreach posts}}
		<article class="im-issue">
			<p class="im-issue-num">{{@number}}</p>
			<p class="im-issue-date">{{date format="D MMM YYYY"}}</p>
			<h3 class="im-issue-title"><a href="{{url}}">{{title}}</a></h3>
			<p class="im-issue-text">{{excerpt words="26"}}</p>
		</article>
		{{/foreach}}
	</div>
{{/get}}
		{{{{/code}}}}
		<p>An issue is an ordinary post with an internal tag. It has a URL, it is in the RSS feed, and search engines can read it — which a newsletter archive locked inside a mail provider is not.</p>
	</div>
</section>
